    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Proposed test with existing data: One could measure energy use and force generation during fertilization, chromosome motion and development, but the assertion that matter acts only as a seat of energy or centre of force has no distinct outcome from ordinary physical descriptions of matter.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-gpt-5.6-sol-medium>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/assessmentType> "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/evidenceAgainst> "Seats of energy and centres of force lack unique modern measurements.", "The word only makes the framing metaphysical rather than a separable mechanism.";
